
There is startapp, but it doesn't transfer stdin/stdout to the program.
For interactive use in clautolisp (and alfe), we introduce the shell escape
character "!".
It is a configurable value shell-escape-character

When a line is input at the REPL (any interactor, lisp, aldo, navi,
sedit), that starts with this shell escape character, the rest of the
line is passed to the $SHELL for interpretation, with
stdin/stdout/stderr inherited.

If the command ends in & the shell will fork a child process, but bash
doesn't display the PID or any job-control instruction in this
(non-interactive) mode. So we must add "echo $!" to the command to
print the pid of the child.

| Example interaction    | What is executed/printed     | Alternative output     |
|------------------------+------------------------------+------------------------|
| _$ !pwd                | bash -c 'pwd'                |                        |
| /Users/pjb/src/ogamita | /Users/pjb/src/ogamita       |                        |
|------------------------+------------------------------+------------------------|
| _$ !pwd &              | bash -c 'pwd & echo $!'      |                        |
| 4819                   | 4819                         | /Users/pjb/src/ogamita |
| /Users/pjb/src/ogamita | /Users/pjb/src/ogamita       | 4819                   |
|------------------------+------------------------------+------------------------|
| _$ !echo hello \       |                              |                        |
| > world.               | bash -c 'echo hello  world.' |                        |
| hello world.           | hello world.                 |                        |
|------------------------+------------------------------+------------------------|

There may not be any space or other character input before the
shell-escape-character.

There may be spaces before or after the shell command, so the test for
& must take into account this possibility.

There may be continuation lines when the preceeding line ends with a
backslash "\".

The "What is executed" column is only an example, it depends on $SHELL
environment variable.
